WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Please welcome Kate Mara.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.320
(audience cheers and applauds)

3
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.290
It's so nice to see you.

4
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:11.290
It's so nice to see you, too, and I can't help it.

5
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.560
I wanna dive right in.

6
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.560
I watched "A Teacher," and I binged it.

7
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.660
The amount of tension I felt in my body watching you

8
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.400
in this character, and it is so brave

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.960
to your outward, your inwards.

10
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.690
There's a tenseness, but you make people feel everything

11
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.690
that you're feeling, and that is so hard to do!

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.303
And you're doing it!

13
00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.820
That is so incredibly generous,

14
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.270
especially coming from you because I respect you so much

15
00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.490
as an actress and a producer.

16
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:55.560
But I know that it's a very specific kind of show,

17
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.360
and it can be hard to watch.

18
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.180
It is a little hard to watch here and there,

19
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.230
but it's riveting, and when you're trying

20
00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.410
to convey what you're feeling on the inside,

21
00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.610
that is so hard to get across, and yet you do.

22
00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.990
How did you do that?

23
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.210 line:15%
That's so nice to hear, but I think that a lot

24
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.530 line:15%
of that is just credit to the writers

25
00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.563 line:15%
and the director, Hannah Fidell.

26
00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:25.960
She was going for a very specific thing,

27
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.350
so I think a lot is unsaid in her work,

28
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.940
and I think with this,

29
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.520
my character Claire's life is internal.

30
00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.930
I think that the show, they're very dynamic

31
00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.710
in its quiet, quiet moments.

32
00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:44.010
That's what I think.

33
00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.630
It's a ride, your performance in this show.

34
00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.283
I felt a lot of anxiety. I felt a lot of empathy.

35
00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.320
I felt it going off the cliff,

36
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.000
but I was riveted watching it.

37
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.200
I wanted to pull it back. It's really good.

38
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.340
It's so well done, and I know you produced this as well.

39
00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.173
Yeah.

40
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.960
It's my first television or I guess streaming thing

41
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.040 line:15%
that I've ever produced.

42
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.740 line:15%
I only produced one other thing,

43
00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:18.400
so I'm still very new at the whole producing aspect

44
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.040
of my career, but it's been so rewarding

45
00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:27.040
to be a part of this from the very beginning, years ago,

46
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.860
and to be able to be so creatively involved

47
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.890
in every aspect of it.

48
00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:38.890
Now family. You are married to Jamie Bell.

49
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.360
Yes, who loves you so much. (laughs)

50
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.470
I love him so much.

51
00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:50.450
I think he is so talented from "Billy Elliott"

52
00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:54.497 line:15%
all the way through, and I know what it's like to grow up

53
00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.880 line:15%
in this wonderful job of ours, and he's done it so well.

54
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.500
By the way, you're an animal lover.

55
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.630
Will you please tell me about Chancey?

56
00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.020
Aw, you're talking about Chancey the chimp. Look at that.

57
00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.280
I had the absolute privilege of being able

58
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.330
to go to Liberia, me and my sister, actually.

59
00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.900
We work with this incredible sanctuary.

60
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:23.950
There he is laughing.

61
00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.820
Our friends run a sanctuary there,

62
00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.820
and it's me and my sister's passion project

63
00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.553
to help get the word out about them.

64
00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:38.460
Liberia Chimpanzee Rescue Protection; they're amazing.

65
00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.520
You should follow them on Instagram,

66
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.163
but they're giving homes to all these baby chimps.

67
00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.210
I would love to post about it and have it on our website.

68
00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:51.580
We'd love to shine a light on that organization.

69
00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.123
Thank you so much for coming on the show.

70
00:03:55.192 --> 00:03:56.357
I am cheering you on.

71
00:03:56.357 --> 00:03:58.721 line:15%
"A Teacher" on FX on Hulu.

72
00:03:58.721 --> 00:04:02.138 line:15%
